This is example text: Our Health Inequalities Team works to better understand and address the avoidable and unfair differences in health experienced by communities. We bring together researchers, healthcare professionals, partner organisations and members of the public to identify where inequalities exist and develop practical, evidence informed approaches to reducing them.

Our work considers the wider factors that shape health, including access to services, socioeconomic circumstances, education, employment, housing, environment and lived experience. By working collaboratively with communities and local partners, we aim to ensure that research and service development reflect the needs and priorities of the people most affected.

This website will provide information about our team, current projects, research findings, events and opportunities to become involved. Further content and resources will be added as the website develops.
